    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      192.69,
      345.61,
      413.13,
      356.68
    ],
    "text": "MERCHANT SHIPPING ACT, No. 52 OF 1971",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      369.61,
      539.75,
      392.68
    ],
    "text": "REGULATIONS made by the Minister of Ports and Shipping under section 321 read with section 44 of the MerchantShipping Act, No. 52 of 1971.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      417.61,
      539.87,
      464.68
    ],
    "text": "ARJUNA RANATUNGA,Minister of Ports and Shipping.Colombo,02nd May 2017.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      275.85,
      477.61,
      329.85,
      488.68
    ],
    "text": "Regulations",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      83.85,
      501.61,
      529.54,
      512.68
    ],
    "text": "1. These regulations may be cited as the Merchant Shipping (Small Commercial Vessels) Regulations, 2017.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      83.85,
      525.61,
      230.88,
      536.68
    ],
    "text": "2. These Regulations shall apply to-",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      96.45,
      549.61,
      539.92,
      584.68
    ],
    "text": "(a) commercial vessels, which are cargo or passenger vessels of not less than five meters and not more thantwenty-four meters in length and which carry not more than 100 passengers or provide overnightaccommodation for not more than twenty-four passengers engaged on coastal waters of Sri Lanka; and",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      95.85,
      597.61,
      287.85,
      608.68
    ],
    "text": "(b) pleasure vessels used for profit or reward.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      621.61,
      539.93,
      656.68
    ],
    "text": "3. Every vessel to which these regulations apply shall not be operated without having on board a valid Certificateof Registration issued by the Registrar of Ships and a valid Certificate of Survey issued by the Director-General MerchantShipping.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      72.37,
      543.87,
      94.38
    ],
    "text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2017'05'04PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA 04.05.20172A",
    "fonts": [
      "FMAbabld,Bold",
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.300000190734863,
      9.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      100.93,
      547.27,
      160.0
    ],
    "text": "4. (1) The Director-General of Merchant Shipping shall, upon the inspection of a vessel of a foreign country,which has similar standards as specified in the Code of Safety for Small Commercial Vessels formulated by the DirectorGeneral of Merchant Shipping accept the certificate of survey or similar certificate to that effect of a vessel of suchforeign country, if such certificate of survey or similar certificate corresponds with the conditions of the vessel and itsequipment.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      172.93,
      547.28,
      208.0
    ],
    "text": "(2) Upon such inspection, where the Director-General of Merchant Shipping finds that such Certificate ofSurvey or similar certificate of a vessel of such foreign country does not correspond with the condition of the vessel,such vessel shall not be registered in Sri Lanka.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      220.93,
      547.2,
      244.0
    ],
    "text": "5. Every person who wishes to register a vessel under these regulations shall apply in the form set out in ScheduleI of these regulations in triplicate accompanied with a fee as specified in Schedule II of these regulations.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      91.15,
      256.93,
      386.38,
      268.0
    ],
    "text": "6. The applicant shall submit the following together with an application-",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      103.75,
      280.93,
      432.58,
      292.0
    ],
    "text": "(a) Certificate of Survey issued by the Director-General of Merchant Shipping;",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      103.15,
      304.93,
      547.19,
      340.0
    ],
    "text": "(b) a comprehensive insurance cover for both P & I and hull and machinery for the vessel obtained from anInsurance Company approved by the Insurance Board of Sri Lanka, covering its crew members, passengersand cargo such vessel is entitled to carry;",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      104.71,
      352.93,
      547.17,
      364.0
    ],
    "text": "(c) the names and the competency of the Boat Master, officers and crew of the vessel and their nationality; and",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      103.15,
      376.93,
      547.2,
      400.0
    ],
    "text": "(d) a written undertaking to inform the Registrar of Ships in relation to any change of any of the informationcontained in the application, within a period of one month of taking place of such change.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      412.93,
      547.25,
      436.0
    ],
    "text": "7. Upon the receipt of the application, the Registrar of Ships shall proceed with the registration of the vessel interms of the provisions of the Merchant Shipping Act, No 52 of 1971 and grant the applicant a Certificate of Registration:",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      448.93,
      547.35,
      484.0
    ],
    "text": "Provided that, if the applicant is unable to produce all the documents referred to above, at the time of hisapplication, the Registrar of Ships may on being satisfied that the failure of submitting of such documents is not due to afault of the applicant-",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      103.75,
      496.93,
      547.21,
      520.0
    ],
    "text": "(a) require the applicant to produce in its place any other relevant document as the Registrar of Ships mayrequire; or",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      103.15,
      532.93,
      393.57,
      544.0
    ],
    "text": "(b) exempt the applicant from the requirement of producing the same,",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      100.15,
      556.93,
      547.22,
      580.0
    ],
    "text": "and proceed to grant the applicant a Provisional Certificate of Registration in respect of such a vessel for aperiod of three months.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      592.93,
      547.2,
      628.0
    ],
    "text": "8. It shall be the duty of the holder of a Provisional Certificate of Registration to submit the necessary documentsrequired for the registration of such vessel without delay. Upon the submission of such documents, the applicant shall, inwriting request the Registrar of Ships to issue a Certificate of Registration.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      640.93,
      547.19,
      688.0
    ],
    "text": "9. The Certificate of Registration issued to any vessel under these regulations shall be valid for a period one year.The Certificate of Survey shall be valid for a period one year in the case of a vessel which carries more than twelvepassengers, and five years for all other vessels from the date of inspection unless revoked, provided that the vesselsuccessfully completes an annual inspection.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.15,
      700.93,
      547.22,
      736.0
    ],
    "text": "10. Every inspection shall be carried out in terms of the Code of Safety for Small Commercial Vessels formulatedby the Director General of Merchant Shipping. The Code of Safety for Small Commercial Vessels deals with generalprovisions, construction, freeboard, stability and watertight integrity, machinery, fire protection, lifesaving equipment,",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      50.13,
      71.17,
      537.81,
      94.38
    ],
    "text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2017'05'04PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA 04.05.20173A",
    "fonts": [
      "FMAbabld,Bold",
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.300000190734863,
      9.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      100.93,
      539.89,
      124.0
    ],
    "text": "miscellaneous systems and equipment operational requirements, licensing of boat masters and engineers, manning andhours of work.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      136.93,
      539.94,
      184.0
    ],
    "text": "11. Where any vessel to which these regulations apply fails to hold on board a valid Certificate of Survey or validinsurance certificate, the owner of such vessel shall be guilty of an offence and on conviction thereof shall be liable to afine of one hundred thousand rupees per day in respect of which the vessel is plied without having on board such certificatesor to imprisonment of either description for a term not exceeding two years.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      83.85,
      196.93,
      248.85,
      208.0
    ],
    "text": "12. These regulations shall not apply to-",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      96.45,
      220.93,
      176.84,
      232.0
    ],
    "text": "(a) fishing vessels;",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      95.85,
      244.93,
      539.92,
      268.0
    ],
    "text": "(b) a vessel holding a valid International Passenger Ship Safety Certificate issued under the provisions of theInternational Convention on the Safety of Life at Sea, 1974, as amended (SOLAS); and",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      95.85,
      280.93,
      539.86,
      304.0
    ],
    "text": "(c) a boat forming part of a vessel lifesaving equipment that is used to carry passengers only in emergenciesor during emergency exercises.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      316.93,
      539.87,
      352.0
    ],
    "text": "13. The provisions of Merchant Shipping (Standards of Training, Certification and Watch Keeping for Seafarers)Regulations, 2016 published in Extraordinary Gazette No. 1987/19 of October 4, 2016 shall not apply to the vessels towhich these regulations apply.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      83.85,
      364.93,
      345.41,
      376.0
    ],
    "text": "14. Unless the context otherwise requires, in these regulations-",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      107.85,
      388.93,
      540.03,
      520.0
    ],
    "text": "\u201cAct\u201d means the Merchant Shipping Act, No. 52 of 1971;\u201cCode of Safety for small commercial vessels\u201d means a document which is formulated in Sri Lanka in linewith IMO guidelines and specifies the standards of construction, freeboard, stability and watertightintegrity, machinery, fire protection, lifesaving equipment, miscellaneous systems and equipmentoperational requirements, licensing of boat masters and engineers, manning and hours of work;\u201cPleasure vessels\u201d means vessels designated as pleasure vessels in the Code of Safety for small commercialvessels;\u201cRegistrar of ships\u201d means the Director-General of Merchant Shipping; and\u201cSmall commercial vessel\u201d means vessels which are cargo, or passenger vessels of less than 24 meters, but5 meters or more in length and which carry not more than 100 passengers or provide overnightaccommodation for up to 24 passengers engaged on coastal waters of Sri Lanka.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      479.85,
      532.93,
      539.85,
      544.0
    ],
    "text": "(Regulation 5)",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      263.85,
      556.93,
      323.85,
      568.0
    ],
    "text": "SCHEDULE I",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
